---
import UtilityWindow from "../layouts/utility-window.astro"
import { SITE_DISPLAY_NAME, getMemberSupportEmail } from "@/lib/site-url"

const pageTitle = `Security & Data Protection | ${SITE_DISPLAY_NAME}`
const pageDescription = `How EBC Flex protects your account and personal information.`
---

<UtilityWindow title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription} canonicalPath="/security">
  <div class="space-y-8">
    <div class="border-b border-[var(--layout-border)] pb-6">
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-[var(--layout-text)] tracking-tight mb-3">Security &amp; Data Protection</h1>
      <p class="text-base text-[var(--layout-muted)] leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        How EBC Flex protects your account and health information.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="text-[var(--layout-text)] leading-relaxed space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--layout-text)]">Protected Access</h2>
      <p class="text-[var(--layout-muted)]">
        Spending accounts hold sensitive health and financial information. Sign-in is protected by
        multi-factor verification, and account activity is monitored for suspicious access so
        attempts to reach your information are blocked before they succeed.
      </p>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--layout-text)]">Practical Steps for Users</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-[var(--layout-muted)]">
        <li>Keep your password unique and your contact details current for verification codes.</li>
        <li>Review card transactions regularly and report anything unfamiliar promptly.</li>
        <li>Never share one-time codes — support will never ask for them by phone or email.</li>
        <li>Sign out on shared devices and keep receipts for your records.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--layout-text)]">Privacy by Design</h2>
      <p class="text-[var(--layout-muted)]">
        Information handling follows data-minimization practices and applicable health privacy
        requirements. Documentation you upload is used to process your claims and is retained only
        as needed for those services and record-keeping obligations.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--layout-text)]">Data Handling Practices</h2>
    <p class="text-[var(--layout-muted)]">
      Data-handling practices follow the principle of collecting only what the service requires,
      keeping it only as long as obligations demand, and limiting internal access to the people and
      systems that need it. These practices are reviewed as regulations and risks evolve, and
      improvements are applied continuously rather than on a fixed schedule.
    </p>
    <p class="text-[var(--layout-muted)]">
      If an incident ever affects your information, notification follows applicable legal
      requirements so you can take protective steps quickly. Your vigilance is the strongest
      complement to these controls.
    </p>
    <p class="text-[var(--layout-muted)]">
      Recognizing the warning signs of fraud matters as much as the technology behind the sign-in
      page. Unexpected urgency, requests for codes or passwords, and links to unfamiliar
      sign-in pages are the most common warning signs. When anything feels wrong, stop and contact
      member support through a channel you know is genuine.
    </p>
    <p class="text-[var(--layout-muted)]">
      Further detail about data handling is available in the Privacy Notice, and the FAQ covers
      common security questions in plain language. Protecting your account is a shared effort, and
      we are glad to help with any concern.
    </p>
  </div>
</UtilityWindow>
